"""One ``Redaction`` table replaces the two rect blobs (issue #240, PR B).

No data is copied: the blobs came from the legacy YOLO trio, and the
compute writes the rows again. For every scan in review 2's two open
statuses the detect ledger's ``apply_run`` is blanked, so the collect
tick (``yolo.queue_ready_runs``) sees the redactions as not current and
queues the compute, which writes the rows within minutes. A closed
review (``REDACTION_REVIEW_DONE``) is not recomputed under the person
who closed it (#263), and a legacy volume has no run: both get no rows.
"""

